                     <provenance type="#c"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_36">Battle, Sussex.
                           Benedictine abbey of St Martin</orgName><p>MS Tiberius B.v, part I, fols.
                           2–73, 77–88 was originally part of the same volume as MS Nero D.ii fols.
                           238–41. MS Tiberius B.v, fol. 88r, contains an 'annotatio ecclesiarum
                           dotalium Ecclesie de Bello' of 1154, and MS Nero D.ii contains Battle
                           Abbey annals.</p></provenance>
                     <provenance type="#c" cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_437">Winchester,
                           Hampshire. Benedictine cathedral priory of St Peter, St Paul, and St
                           Swithun</orgName><p>For provenance, compare contents. '[S]UUIÐHUN' in
                           capitals in a list of bishops.</p></provenance>
                     <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_224">Glastonbury,
                           Somerset, Benedictine Abbey of Saint Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>Contains
                           Glastonbury material, for example the earlier part of the manuscript
                           includes a list of the abbots, but Winchester, St Swithun's seems on the
                           whole more likely (see above).</p></provenance>
                     <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName role="fmo">Sir Robert Bruce
